    "problems": "The paper does not measure held-out cross-entropy or perplexity for its six models, and its connection from margin geometry to loss scaling is presented as an interpretation rather than a tested result. The models span 124M–1.5B parameters, not several orders of magnitude of loss-scaling experiments; no compute or token-budget sweep is reported.",
    "rows_left_out": "No claim-version results were available to extract. Margin-distribution percentiles in Table 4 and other geometric results are omitted because they do not add a separate direct measurement relevant to the scaling-law claim beyond the recorded proxy outcomes.",
